From 8088279c7ad8f083ac87361c1587ae234728250f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 22:30:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] fix: v0.43 server, round 1 (notePresent; the event
 handlers table; one Tx; RollCampaign; keptLabel)

S-1 (R1.3.5's notePresent): a player noted present is notePresent(campaignId), beside noting in
src/lib/routes/seat-routes.ts, which already imports notePlayersSeen (still mocked at
@/db/roll-requests): the table's, the companion table's and the party sheet's calls, with the
table's words, and the notes', with its own. noting is file-private now. It sits beside noting,
not in http.ts, so http.ts keeps no database import and seat-routes and http.ts don't import
each other.

S-2 (R1.3.8's EVENT_HANDLERS): apply's switch is EVENT_HANDLERS in src/db/campaign-events.ts,
an event type's handler given its payload and what applying needs (tx, campaign, session,
sentAt, drawings). The cases are copied as they were, in the same order, with the same writes;
the types that shared a case share a named handler (keepMessage, keepCombat, keepCombatant), and
a command's or a dish's result, which the events route records itself, has none and answers
false as before. The table is typed by a payload map (EventData), so neither the table nor apply
needs a cast.

S-5: inRoster is file-private (its only caller is createCommand). S-6: db/notes.ts's two
`Prisma.TransactionClient` are Tx. S-7: the roll path's campaign payload is named once,
RollCampaign, beside ROLL_CAMPAIGN; and commands' gmLabel() is keptLabel(), apart from
ROLL_KIND_INFO's gmLabel field, at its three callers.

No request, answer, stored row or Prisma argument changes. L1 (l1/S/fix1, on this tree over
a2332a2 with commits 9-11): jest 306 suites, 9698 tests, 0 red; typegen, tsc 0 errors; eslint 0
errors, 608 warnings; gates 1-12 ok (gate 9 608 against 981, gate 12 two cycle groups, base
four; gate 4b checks 698 names, as three route modules no longer import notePlayersSeen).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01821Sr9FKASxJn47SNudpbR
